From d2a8c5cbf25f66623ff9cb0e7daa85f30ae2db39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:45:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): refresh pacing before local admission [daveey]

Remote-pool notices reject stale usage correctly, but admission-only reads leave capped or ineligible hubs without a natural producer. Refresh configured pools during pre-cap maintenance through the existing shared/memory usage budget. Preserve disabled/dry-run behavior, failure UNKNOWN, and read-only stale rejection. No warning classifier, admission math or rollout configuration changes.

Recovered producer scope from 9d980300045d; excluded classifier scope owned by PR3268. RED: three idle/remote-only/failure assertions fail on main. GREEN: 131 focused tests across seven consumers. Whole scripts/check: 20 checks green. Detection gap closed with remote-only ready work and zero-admission cadence tests, failed-read persisted/memory budgets, disable/dry-run and 900s stale control. Live acceptance remains gated on authorized rollout and installed real-card proof.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_dispatch_maintenance.py     |   2 +
 hermes_cli/kanban_llm_pacing_dispatch.py      |  25 +++-
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_llm_pacing.py    |  11 +-
 .../test_kanban_pacing_idle_tick.py           | 128 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../hermes_cli/test_kanban_pacing_recovery.py |   2 +
 5 files changed, 159 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
